#: src/introduction.md:32
msgid "A note on output"
msgstr "Eng Notiz zum Output"

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid ""
"goat is built to be both a pleasure to use _and_ safe to script. Friendly "
"touches — a 🐐 when everything's green, a hint about your next step — only "
"ever appear on an interactive terminal. Pipe goat into a script or ask for "
"`--json` and you get clean, stable, machine-readable output with nothing "
"decorative in the way. Set `GOAT_NO_FUN=1` and even the interactive "
"flourishes go quiet."
msgstr ""
"goat ass gebaut fir souwuel e Plëséier ze benotzen _ewéi_ och sécher ze "
"scripten. Frëndlech Akzenter — e 🐐 wann alles gréng ass, en Hiweis op däin "
"nächste Schrëtt — erschéngen nëmmen op engem interaktiven Terminal. Pipe "
"goat an e Script oder freet `--json` un an du kriss propperen, stabilen, "
"maschinneliesbaren Output ouni eppes Dekoratives am Wee. Setz "
"`GOAT_NO_FUN=1` an och déi interaktiv Verzierungen gi roueg."

#: src/getting-started.md:3
msgid ""
"You don't need a profile, a bundle, or a network to start. goat ships with a "
"sandbox so you can learn by doing, safely."
msgstr ""
"Du brauchs kee Profil, kee Bündel a kee Netzwierk fir unzefänken. goat kënnt "
"mat enger Sandbox sou datt s du sécher duerch Maachen léiere kanns."

#: src/getting-started.md:5
msgid "1. Say hello"
msgstr "1. Sot hello"

#: src/getting-started.md:11
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simulated fabric, no real mesh. Run `goat init` to attach a real "
"env.\n"
"goat hello — saying `lo` to the fabric as `default` on topic `hello/"
"default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     accepted topic `hello/default` (simulated)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     routed `lo` to `hello/default` over the WireGuard "
"P2P path (simulated)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber your subscriber received `lo` — round-trip complete "
"(simulated)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: the first message ever sent over a network (ARPANET, 29 Oct 1969) "
"— they typed \"LOGIN\" and the link crashed after two letters.\n"
"round-trip complete.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simuléiert Fabric, kee richtege Mesh. Laf `goat init` fir eng "
"richteg env unzehänken.\n"
"goat hello — seet `lo` zur Fabric als `default` um Topic `hello/default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     huet Topic `hello/default` ugeholl (simuléiert)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     huet `lo` op `hello/default` iwwer de WireGuard P2P-"
"Wee geleet (simuléiert)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber däin Abonnent huet `lo` kritt — Round-Trip "
"ofgeschloss (simuléiert)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: déi éischt Noriicht déi jee iwwer e Netzwierk geschéckt gouf "
"(ARPANET, 29. Okt 1969) — si hunn \"LOGIN\" getippt an d'Verbindung ass no "
"zwee Buschtawen ofgestierzt.\n"
"Round-Trip ofgeschloss.\n"
"```"

#: src/getting-started.md:21
msgid ""
"`goat hello` publishes a message, subscribes to it, and watches it come back "
"— narrating every hop the data took. In the sandbox those hops are "
"simulated; against a real env they're real. Either way, when it says _round-"
"trip complete_, you know the path works end to end."
msgstr ""
"`goat hello` publizéiert eng Noriicht, abonnéiert se, a kuckt wéi se "
"zréckkënnt — beschreift all Hop deen d'Daten geholl hunn. An der Sandbox "
"sinn déi Hops simuléiert; géint eng richteg env si se richteg. Egal wéi, "
"wann et _Round-Trip ofgeschloss_ seet, weess du datt de Wee vun Enn zu Enn "
"funktionéiert."

#: src/getting-started.md:23
msgid ""
"The message is `lo` on purpose — the first thing ever sent over a network."
msgstr ""
"D'Noriicht ass mat Absicht `lo` — dat éischt wat jee iwwer e Netzwierk "
"geschéckt gouf."

#: src/getting-started.md:25
msgid "2. Take the tour"
msgstr "2. Maach d'Tour"

#: src/getting-started.md:31
msgid ""
"`goat tutor` is a self-paced, hands-on tour — think `vimtutor` for the "
"fabric. Eight short lessons take you from \"what is this\" to publishing, "
"subscribing, diagnosing, and reading the substrate cascade. It runs in the "
"sandbox by default, saves your place, and you can stop and resume any time:"
msgstr ""
"`goat tutor` ass eng selbstgesteiert, praktesch Tour — denk u `vimtutor` fir "
"d'Fabric. Aacht kuerz Lektiounen huelen dech vu \"wat ass dat\" bis zum "
"Publizéieren, Abonnéieren, Diagnostizéieren a Liesen vun der Substrat-"
"Kaskad. Et leeft standardméisseg an der Sandbox, späichert däi Plaz, an du "
"kanns zu all Moment ophalen a weiderfueren:"

#: src/getting-started.md:39
msgid "3. Attach a real environment"
msgstr "3. Hänk eng richteg Ëmgéigend un"

#: src/getting-started.md:41
msgid ""
"When you've been issued an onboarding **bundle** (a `.cbor` file with your "
"identity), the wizard takes it from here:"
msgstr ""
"Wann s du en Onboarding-**Bündel** kritt hues (eng `.cbor`-Datei mat denger "
"Identitéit), iwwerhëlt den Assistent vun hei:"

#: src/getting-started.md:49
msgid ""
"`goat init` is the friendly front door — it detects whether you're set up, "
"lets you choose the sandbox or a real env, proves it works, and points you "
"at the tutor. `goat doctor` then runs a stepped reachability check (mesh → "
"router → certificate → portal) and, if anything's wrong, tells you exactly "
"what to fix."
msgstr ""
"`goat init` ass déi frëndlech Virdier — et erkennt ob s du ageriicht bass, "
"léisst dech d'Sandbox oder eng richteg env wielen, beweist datt et "
"funktionéiert, a weist dech op den Tutor. `goat doctor` leeft duerno e "
"gestaffelten Erreechbarkeetstest (mesh → router → certificate → portal) a, "
"wann eppes verkéiert ass, seet der genau wat ze fléckt ass."

#: src/getting-started.md:51
msgid ""
"When all of doctor's steps pass, you'll see a small 🐐 — you're on the "
"fabric."
msgstr ""
"Wann all Schrëtt vum doctor duerchkommen, gesäis du e klenge 🐐 — du bass op "
"der Fabric."

#: src/getting-started.md:53
msgid "Where to next"
msgstr "Wuer als nächst"

#: src/getting-started.md:55
msgid "New to the ideas? Read **[How the fabric works](concepts.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Nei bei den Iddien? Lies **[Wéi d'Fabric funktionéiert](concepts.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:56
msgid "Ready to do things? Jump to **[Everyday tasks](everyday.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Prett fir Saachen ze maachen? Spréng op **[Alldeeglech Aufgaben]"
"(everyday.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:57
msgid "Something not working? **[Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md)**."
msgstr "Eppes funktionéiert net? **[Problemléisung](troubleshooting.md)**."

#: src/concepts.md:3
msgid ""
"You can use goat productively with just three ideas: **identity**, "
"**topics**, and **no broker**. Here they are."
msgstr ""
"Du kanns goat produktiv mat just dräi Iddie benotzen: **Identitéit**, "
"**Topiken** an **keen Broker**. Hei sinn se."

#: src/concepts.md:5
msgid "A mesh you join with an identity"
msgstr "E Mesh deem s du mat enger Identitéit bäitriets"

#: src/concepts.md:7
msgid ""
"The fabric is a self-healing mesh. Peers connect **directly** to each other "
"over encrypted WireGuard tunnels — once you're enrolled, your data doesn't "
"route through a central server, and your connections survive a management-"
"plane outage or a flaky uplink."
msgstr ""
"D'Fabric ass e selbstheelende Mesh. Peers verbannen sech **direkt** mateneen "
"iwwer verschlësselte WireGuard-Tunnelen — soubal s du ageschriwwe bass, "
"leeft däin Datentransfert net iwwer e zentrale Server, an deng Verbindunge "
"iwwerliewen e Management-Plane-Ausfall oder en onbestännegen Uplink."

#: src/concepts.md:9
msgid ""
"You join with an **identity**: an onboarding _bundle_ that carries your "
"certificate, an access token, and where the fabric lives. The fabric admits "
"you by _who you are_, not by a shared password. `goat profile init "
"<bundle.cbor>` installs that identity; you can hold several under different "
"_contexts_ and switch between them."
msgstr ""
"Du trëtts mat enger **Identitéit** bäi: en Onboarding-_Bündel_ deen däin "
"Zertifikat, en Access-Token an d'Plaz wou d'Fabric lieft mat sech dréit. "
"D'Fabric léisst dech eran no _wien s du bass_, net no engem gedeelte "
"Passwuert. `goat profile init <bundle.cbor>` installéiert déi Identitéit; du "
"kanns der e puer ënner verschiddene _Kontexter_ halen an tëscht hinnen "
"wiesselen."

#: src/concepts.md:19
msgid "Topics: publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Topiken: publizéieren an abonnéieren"

#: src/concepts.md:21
msgid ""
"Data moves on **topics** — slash-delimited paths like `acme/radar1/tracks`. "
"The model is publish/subscribe:"
msgstr ""
"Daten beweege sech op **Topiken** — Schrägstrich-getrennte Pied wéi `acme/"
"radar1/tracks`. D'Modell ass publish/subscribe:"

#: src/concepts.md:23
msgid "**Publish** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) writes a value to a topic."
msgstr ""
"**Publish** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) schreift e Wäert op en Topic."

#: src/concepts.md:24
msgid ""
"**Subscribe** (`goat sub <topic>`) receives every value published there, "
"live, as long as you're allowed to read it."
msgstr ""
"**Subscribe** (`goat sub <topic>`) kritt all Wäert deen do publizéiert gëtt, "
"live, sou laang wéi s du em liese duerfs."

#: src/concepts.md:26
msgid ""
"A topic is just a name; you create it (`goat topic create`), publish to it, "
"and anyone permitted can subscribe. `goat hello` is simply a publish and a "
"subscribe wired together so you can watch a value make the round trip."
msgstr ""
"En Topic ass just en Numm; du erstells en (`goat topic create`), publizéiers "
"drop, an all dee berechtegt ass ka subscriben. `goat hello` ass einfach e "
"Publish an e Subscribe zesummegehaangen sou datt s du e Wäert beim Round-"
"Trip kucke kanns."

#: src/concepts.md:28
msgid "No broker — and why that matters"
msgstr "Keen Broker — a firwat dat wichteg ass"

#: src/concepts.md:30
msgid ""
"There is **no central broker** sitting in the middle of the data path. When "
"you publish, the value flows over the mesh directly to the peers subscribed "
"to it. That's deliberate: it removes the single bottleneck and single point "
"of failure that a broker would be."
msgstr ""
"Et gëtt **keen zentrale Broker** deen an der Mëtt vum Datewee sëtzt. Wann s "
"du publizéiers, fléisst de Wäert iwwer de Mesh direkt zu de Peers déi en "
"abonnéiert hunn. Dat ass mat Absicht: et entfernt den eenzege Flaschenhals "
"an deen eenzege Feelerpunkt deen e Broker wier."

#: src/concepts.md:32
msgid ""
"A practical consequence: **reads are broad, writes are the cut.** Being able "
"to _read_ a topic is permissive by design; _writing_ to one is governed by "
"your identity. So you'll rarely be surprised by what you can subscribe to, "
"and the integrity of what's published is anchored to who published it."
msgstr ""
"Eng praktesch Konsequenz: **Lesen ass breed, Schreiwen ass den "
"Trennstréch.** En Topic _liese_ kënnen ass per Design erlaabt; op een "
"_schreiwen_ gëtt vun denger Identitéit geregelt. Also wäerts du seele "
"iwwerrascht sinn vun deem wat s du abonnéiere kanns, an d'Integritéit vun "
"deem wat publizéiert gëtt ass verankert u wien et publizéiert huet."

#: src/concepts.md:34
msgid "Sandbox vs. real"
msgstr "Sandbox vs. richteg"

#: src/concepts.md:36
msgid ""
"Everything above has a faithful **in-process simulation** — the sandbox. "
"`goat hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox`, and `goat tutor` exercise the "
"same shapes (a topic, a publish, a round-trip, a verdict) with no network "
"and no identity, so you can learn the model before you touch the real "
"fabric. The sandbox always says so with a `◇ SANDBOX` banner, and it never "
"writes to or reads from a real mesh."
msgstr ""
"Alles uewen huet eng getrei **in-process Simulatioun** — d'Sandbox. `goat "
"hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox` an `goat tutor` üben déiselwecht "
"Formen (en Topic, e Publish, e Round-Trip, en Uerteel) ouni Netzwierk an "
"ouni Identitéit, sou datt s du d'Modell léiere kanns ier s du déi richteg "
"Fabric ureeft. D'Sandbox seet et ëmmer mat engem `◇ SANDBOX` Banner, an et "
"schreift ni op e richtege Mesh oder liest dovun."

#: src/concepts.md:38
msgid ""
"When you switch to a real env, the _commands don't change_ — only the "
"backing does."
msgstr ""
"Wann s du op eng richteg env wiesselt, _änneren d'Befehler net_ — nëmmen dat "
"wat dohannert ass ännert sech."

#: src/concepts.md:40
msgid ""
"Want the deeper architecture (the relay fallback, the access model, the "
"audit trail)? Ask your goat administrator for the design references — this "
"guide stays focused on operating the CLI."
msgstr ""
"Wëlls du déi déifer Architektur (de Relay-Fallback, d'Zougangsmodell, "
"d'Audit-Trail)? Frot däi goat-Administrateur no den Design-Referenzen — dëse "
"Guide bleift op d'Bedéngen vum CLI fokusséiert."

#: src/everyday.md:3
msgid ""
"The commands you'll actually reach for, as quick recipes. Add `--help` to "
"any of them for the full set of flags, or see the **[Command reference]"
"(reference.md)**."
msgstr ""
"D'Befehler no deenen s du tatsächlech grëfft, als séier Rezepter. Setz `--"
"help` zu engem dovunner fir de ganze Set vu Flags, oder kuck "
"d'**[Befehlsreferenz](reference.md)**."

#: src/everyday.md:5
msgid "Check you're connected"
msgstr "Iwwerpréif ob s du verbonne bass"

#: src/everyday.md:12
msgid ""
"`goat doctor` is your first stop whenever something feels off — each step "
"that fails prints a specific remediation. When everything's green, both "
"commands give you a clear all-clear."
msgstr ""
"`goat doctor` ass däin éischte Stopp wann eppes komesch schéngt — all "
"Schrëtt deen feelt weist eng spezifesch Behiewung. Wann alles gréng ass, "
"ginn dir béid Befehler e kloert Alles-an-Uerdnung."

#: src/everyday.md:14
msgid "Publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Publizéieren an abonnéieren"

#: src/everyday.md:16
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # watch a topic live (Ctrl-C to "
"stop)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # a whole subtree\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # publish a payload\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # en Topic live kucken (Ctrl-C fir "
"ophalen)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # e ganzen Ënnerbaam\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # eng Payload publizéieren\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:22
msgid "Want to see the ripple a publish sets off? Add `--narrate`:"
msgstr ""
"Wëlls du d'Welle gesinn déi e Publish ausléist? Setz `--narrate` derbäi:"

#: src/everyday.md:24
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:28
msgid "Work with topics"
msgstr "Mat Topiken schaffen"

#: src/everyday.md:30
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # list topics\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # drill into an org/prefix\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # one topic's full record\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # Topiken oplëschten\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # an eng Organisatioun/prefix "
"erabueren\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # de ganze Record vun engem "
"Topic\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:37
msgid ""
"After you create a topic, goat nudges you toward the natural next step "
"(watch it, or publish to it)."
msgstr ""
"Nodeems s du en Topic erstellt hues, schubst dech goat zum natierlechen "
"nächste Schrëtt (kuck en, oder publizéier drop)."

#: src/everyday.md:39
msgid "Diagnose a problem"
msgstr "E Problem diagnostizéieren"

#: src/everyday.md:47
msgid ""
"`inspect` returns findings and the remedy for each — what's wrong and what "
"to do about it."
msgstr ""
"`inspect` gëtt Befunde zréck an d'Behiewung fir jiddwereen — wat verkéiert "
"ass a wat dergéint ze maachen ass."

#: src/everyday.md:49
msgid "Scripting"
msgstr "Scripting"

#: src/everyday.md:51
msgid ""
"Every command that prints a human view also offers `--json` for a stable, "
"machine-readable one. The JSON form never carries banners, hints, or "
"flourishes, and its shape and your exit code stay constant across releases "
"and languages:"
msgstr ""
"All Befehl deen eng mënschlech Vue weist bitt och `--json` fir eng stabil, "
"maschinneliesbar. D'JSON-Form dréit ni Banneren, Hiweiser oder Verzierungen, "
"an hir Form an däin Exit-Code bleiwe konstant iwwer Releases a Sproochen "
"ewech:"

#: src/everyday.md:58
msgid "This is the contract: **friendly on a terminal, clean in a pipe.**"
msgstr ""
"Dat ass de Kontrakt: **frëndlech op engem Terminal, propper an enger Pipe.**"

#: src/everyday.md:60
msgid ""
"One caution: `goat status` opens a real session at the router each time it runs, so it is a check you run when you want an answer, not something to poll from a timer. For a trend over time use `goat health` or `goat top`, which read what the goatnet already publishes."
msgstr ""
"Eng Warnung: `goat status` mécht bei all Lafen eng richteg Sessioun um Router op, et ass also eng Kontroll, déi s du leefs, wann s du eng Äntwert wëlls, näischt, wat en Timer reegelméisseg ofrufft. Fir en Trend iwwer d'Zäit benotz `goat health` oder `goat top`, déi liesen, wat de goatnet souwisou publizéiert."

#: src/install.md:3
msgid ""
"goat is a single self-contained binary — no runtime, no dependencies. It's "
"served mesh-internally from `get.<your-goatnet>` (you're already on the mesh "
"if you can read this), and the version here always matches the binary that "
"surface serves."
msgstr ""
"goat ass ee selbststännegt Binär — keng Runtime, keng Ofhängegkeeten. Et "
"gëtt mesh-intern vu `get.<your-goatnet>` geliwwert (du bass scho um Mesh "
"wann s du dat hei liese kanns), an d'Versioun hei entsprécht ëmmer dem Binär "
"deen déi Surface liwwert."

#: src/install.md:5
msgid "Quick install"
msgstr "Séier Installatioun"

#: src/install.md:7
msgid "**macOS / Linux**"
msgstr "**macOS / Linux**"

#: src/install.md:10
msgid ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"

#: src/install.md:11
msgid "$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"

#: src/install.md:12
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:17
msgid "Make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your `PATH`."
msgstr "Vergewëssert iech datt `~/.local/bin` op ärem `PATH` ass."

#: src/install.md:19
msgid "**Windows (PowerShell)**"
msgstr "**Windows (PowerShell)**"

#: src/install.md:21
msgid ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"

#: src/install.md:26
msgid ""
"Every subcommand works on Windows except `goat client` (the local tunnel "
"daemon), which is Linux/macOS-only."
msgstr ""
"All Ënnerbefehl funktionéiert op Windows ausser `goat client` (de lokalen "
"Tunnel-Daemon), deen nëmme Linux/macOS ass."

#: src/install.md:28
msgid "Verify the download (recommended)"
msgstr "Den Download verifizéieren (recommandéiert)"

#: src/install.md:30
msgid ""
"The download surface publishes a per-binary `*.sha256` and an aggregate "
"`SHA256SUMS`. For a high-assurance install, verify before you run:"
msgstr ""
"D'Download-Surface publizéiert e `*.sha256` pro Binär an en aggregéierten "
"`SHA256SUMS`. Fir eng héich-sécher Installatioun, verifizéier ier s du leefs:"

#: src/install.md:33
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>\""

#: src/install.md:34
msgid "\"$BASE/SHA256SUMS\""
msgstr "\"$BASE/SHA256SUMS\""

#: src/install.md:35
msgid "\"$BASE/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"$BASE/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:35
msgid "# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c   ·   Linux: sha256sum -c\n"
msgstr "# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c   ·   Linux: sha256sum -c\n"

